From ec485c39093f1274e712ca759a08c69afa5b4100 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.local>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:37:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] UPKEEP U4: make IA32_APIC_BASE a real register (LAPIC
 relocation + EN)

WRMSR 0x1B was sparse storage: the MMIO window never moved, the
global enable gated nothing, and every vCPU powered up claiming
BSP (D1 in docs/plans/UPKEEP_PLAN.md). Measured from Intel SDM
Vol.3A ss.10.4.3-10.4.5/10.4.7 and QEMU master hw/intc/apic.c +
apic_common.c:

- One "LAPIC" MMIO region mirrors the current context's MSR
  decode; re-synced on accepted WRMSR, live-pair reset,
  vcpu_load and snapshot load. Per-vCPU window addresses with
  a single registration (SDM 10.4.5); handlers decode against
  the live base.
- WRMSR 0x1B validates before storing: reserved bits (0-7, 9),
  the x2APIC EN bit (unsupported, CPUID.1:ECX[21]=0) and bits
  beyond MAXPHYADDR=40 reject the write with state untouched
  (logged; no #GP, matching the permissive house MSR lane).
  The BSP bit is a strap: writes preserve it (QEMU), and
  cpu_reset seeds it by slot identity (context 0 is the BSP).
- EN=0 is SDM's "no on-chip APIC": the window unmaps,
  CPUID.1:EDX[9] reads 0, IOAPIC/MSI/IPI fixed messages drop
  at the latch, the timer freezes mid-count, delivery stops,
  INIT/SIPI stay reachable. Register state persists across
  the disable except the SVR software-enable (QEMU's choice
  inside SDM's "may be lost"); QEMU's looser EN=0 MMIO-write
  and IRR-latching was measured and not copied. INIT now
  preserves the MSR (QEMU apic_init_reset does not touch it).
- Snapshot load rebinds the window from the restored MSR
  before the MMIO-map check, so a relocated or disabled
  LAPIC restores and continues equivalently; no format change,
  no machine_t movement.

Vectors: four new groups in tests/test_lapic.c driving real
guest WRMSR code (relocation + return with old-window closure,
7 rejected-write shapes, disable/freeze/re-enable incl. timer
resume and end-to-end delivery of a pre-disable latch, SMP
role identity with a window that follows the context switch)
and both snapshot cases in tests/test_snapshot.c. NC: the new
tests on the 0094 archive tree abort at the first U4 assertion
(test_lapic) and show exactly the 9 U4 snapshot FAILs.
make test (stock SeaBIOS ISO lanes present) and
make test-sanitize are green; all K/SMP receipts unchanged.
